{{#step}}
Create the R2 bucket that holds the media and the page cache, declining Wrangler's offer to add the binding itself as in step 1. A Cloudflare account that never used R2 refuses it with error `10042` (`Please enable R2 through the Cloudflare Dashboard`): enable R2 at `https://dash.cloudflare.com/<account id>/r2/overview` first (`wrangler whoami` prints the account id), then run the command again.

   ```bash
   {{#inDirectory "apps" (deployAppDir)}}{{installedBinaryRunner}} wrangler r2 bucket create {{projectName}}-storage --no-update-config{{/inDirectory}}
   ```
{{/step}}
